  "body": "Found while fixing #1232 (PR #1265): the new post-serves-kind check judges a user's OWN post script by the dialect its manifest declares. A plasma script declares the same dialect shape as a milling script, so a user's own plasma script isn't told apart by kind: it could post a plasma (torch) program on a mill setup, or a milling program could pass on a plasma table through a user's own script, without the by-name refusal shipped posts get.\n\nDone means: a user's post script states its machine kind(s) (a manifest key, e.g. serves: [plasma]) that the check reads, and a script that doesn't state it is refused on a kind it can't be proven to serve; pinned with a user plasma script on a mill and a user mill script on a plasma table.\n",
